From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam <i@noc.cat>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:38:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] main: wait for the handover only after the remoteprocs
 started

efi_late_ebs() returned as soon as pil_finish_all() succeeded and only
reached the handover delay when starting the remoteprocs had failed.
The delay itself was 500 seconds, not the intended half second: Stall()
counts microseconds.

Return the error when starting fails, and otherwise give the remoteprocs
500 ms to finish their handover before ExitBootServices() completes.
---
 src/main.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
index 8262564..d77c8c8 100644
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -17,15 +17,15 @@ static EFI_STATUS efi_late_ebs(void)
 
 	status = pil_finish_all();
 	if (status == EFI_NOT_FOUND)
-		return EFI_SUCCESS; /* No rempteprocs found */
-	if (!EFI_ERROR(status))
+		return EFI_SUCCESS; /* No remoteprocs found */
+	if (EFI_ERROR(status))
 		return status;
 
 	/*
 	 * Wait a bit to let remoteprocs finish handover.
 	 * FIXME: Wait for the SMP2P signals instead
 	 */
-	return BS->Stall(500 * 1000 * 1000);
+	return BS->Stall(500 * 1000);
 }
 
 static EFI_STATUS efi_dtb_changed(void)
